# cppcheck suppression baseline.
#
# This file is the frozen baseline for the cppcheck gate (see
# docs/quality.md, issue #76). New findings should be fixed, not
# suppressed; a suppression is acceptable only when the finding is a
# false positive or not applicable to this codebase, and must carry a
# one-line justification next to it.
#
# Format: [file:]id[:line], e.g.:
#   src/core/pipeline.c:uninitVariable
#
# Current baseline: empty. The codebase passes
#   cppcheck --enable=warning,performance,portability --std=c11
#   -I include --include=tooling/cppcheck/preinclude.h
#   --inline-suppr --suppress=missingIncludeSystem --error-exitcode=1
# with zero findings. The CI and devenv commands expand this file into
# --suppress arguments (one per non-comment line) so they work on both old
# and new cppcheck versions.
#
# Note: CI installs cppcheck from the runner's apt repository, so the
# effective version can drift from the one used locally. If a version
# bump introduces new findings, triage them (fix or justify a
# suppression here) before re-freezing.
